## Context

Ticket [[0874]] migrated 339 lines and deposited all 304 discovery link
candidates in `data/jetp/migration/0874-link-candidates.csv`. The 55 records
in `data/jetp/migration/0874-pending.csv` cannot yet name one place in a
collected source snapshot: five source claims and 19 links have no collected
snapshot; 31 links have a snapshot but no precise locator. The author chose
on 2026-09-24 to leave missing snapshots pending until acquisition.

## Work

- Acquire each missing source through the established JETP collection path,
  preserving a retrieval and its byte-addressed snapshot.
- Inspect each vague locator against its stored bytes and record a page,
  section, heading or sentence that identifies the assertion. Never use the
  whole document as a locator.
- Re-run `scripts/jetp/build_lines.py`, inspect every newly minted line, and
  update the pending and candidate files. Preserve M1a served view bytes.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every pending claim and link has a traceable line or an explicit,
  documented absence of available source bytes.
- [ ] The Reuters Cirebon snapshot `9803416b…` is present in the store, or its
  absence is documented, and `idn-impl-cirebon-suspended-2025` leaves
  `0876-pending.csv` and `1160-citation-decisions.csv` with a decision (ticket 1590)
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, M1a byte comparison, `make check-fast`, and
  `make lint` pass.
